[01:06.62] I am on an open sea
[01:09.26] Just drifting as the hours go slowly by
[01:21.42] Julie with her open blouse
[01:24.32] Is gazing up into the empty sky
[01:35.96] Now it seems to be so strange here
[01:50.50] Now it's so blue
[01:59.32] The still sea is darker than before...
[03:10.18] No wind disturbs our coloured sail
[03:13.50] The radio is silent, so are we
[03:25.46] Julie's head is on her arm
[03:28.30] Her fingers brush the surface of the sea
[03:39.96] Now I wonder if we'll be seen here
[03:52.58] Or if time has left us all alone
[04:03.78] The still sea is darker than before...
